/main-forum/scion/989633-netjer-preview-is-up?p=990838#post990838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Loki, mother of Sleipnir, doesn't really have a lot of room to talk.<br /> <br /> I've heard that there's a possibility that the whole barb-spitting thing was added later, although I don't have enough information to fully support that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Loki has personally given birth no less than three times. Coupled with his insult, methinks the mare doth protest too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T01:18:40-07:00","id":990851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989633-netjer-preview-is-up?p=990847#post990847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Loki has personally given birth no less than three times. Coupled with his insult, methinks the mare doth protest too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of continuing to sidetrack this thread about the Netjer, who were the other two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:22:45-07:00","id":990867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989633-netjer-preview-is-up?p=990851#post990851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of continuing to sidetrack this thread about the Netjer, who were the other two?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Loki also give birth to the Jormungandr and Fenrir too? There's also Hel, but I don't know if Loki gave birth to Hel or if he was her father.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:27:03-07:00","id":990869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989633-netjer-preview-is-up?p=990851#post990851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of continuing to sidetrack this thread about the Netjer, who were the other two?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from foaling Sleipnir off of Svadilfari there are also some lines of the Lokasenna where Odin refers to another incident in which Loki played a female role. Loki is described as having spent eight winters in some underground area, either milking cows, or depending on the translator, being milked/lactating. The closing lines of the same stanza accuse Loki of giving birth. <br /> <br /> There's also this from the Lesser Voluspa:<br /> <br /> The wolf did Loki sire on Angrboda, <br /> And Sleipnir he bore to Svadilfari; <br /> The worst piece of witchcraft seemed the one <br /> Sprung from the brother of Byleist then. <br /> A heart ate Loki\u2014in the embers it lay, <br /> And half-cooked found he the woman\u2019s heart- <br /> With child from the woman Lopt soon was, <br /> And thence among men came every troll-woman.<br /> <br /> The phrase troll-woman is, as I understand it, a translation of the word flag\u00f0, which can also be translated as ogress, giantess, witch, she-wolf, etc.Basically anything nasty for a woman to be. Then there is:<br /> <br /> The war I remember, the first in the world, <br /> When the gods with spears had smitten Gullveig, <br /> And in the hall of H\u00e1r had burned her, <br /> Three times burned, and three times born, <br /> Oft and again, yet ever she lives. <br /> Heid they named her <br /> When she came to the house, <br /> The wide-seeing witch, <br /> In magic wise; <br /> She performed sei\u00f0 where she could, <br /> Worked sei\u00f0 in a trance, <br /> To evil women <br /> She was always a joy.<br /> <br /> So we're told that the witch lives and goes around teaching scary magic proper women shouldn't know, whereas in the other it's suggested that Loki ate up her heart and gave birth from it. You could even argue that the witch in question 'is' Loki under a mantle as the Mother of Witches.<br /> <br /> I couldn't find the third instance, I might have been confusing it with the witch being three times born, but in any case giving birth twice is twice more than most men manage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:27:43-07:00","id":990870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989633-netjer-preview-is-up?p=990867#post990867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't Loki also give birth to the Jormungandr and Fenrir too? There's also Hel, but I don't know if Loki gave birth to Hel or if he was her father.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenris, Jormungandr and Hela were sired off of Angrboda, the hag of the Ironwood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:33:15-07:00","id":990871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/989633-netjer-preview-is-up?p=990867#post990867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't Loki also give birth to the Jormungandr and Fenrir too? There's also Hel, but I don't know if Loki gave birth to Hel or if he was her father.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angrbo%C3%B0a\" target=\"_blank\">Angrbo\u00f0a</a> is the mother of Jormungandr, Fenrir, and Hel. Loki is their father. At least that's my understanding of the mythology, which wiki agrees with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T03:29:37-07:00","id":990879,"title":"","content":"Well I stand DOUBLE-corrected. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid